ame":"length","type":"INT","widget":{"name":"length"},"link":14}],"outputs":[{"localized_name":"positive","name":"positive","type":"CONDITIONING","links":[8]},{"localized_name":"LATENT","name":"LATENT","type":"LATENT","links":[7]}],"title":"PROMPT — IMAGE TO VIDEO","properties":{"Node name for S&R":"MiniMaxH3ImageToVideo","cnr_id":"comfy-core","ver":"0.30.0"},"widgets_values":["One frozen instant. Only the camera moves, performing a smooth, continuous 360-degree orbit around a completely motionless subject.\n\nThe subject is a perfectly static, photorealistic 3D capture, not a living, animated person. Every facial feature is permanently frozen in its exact original position and expression throughout the entire shot.\n\n**CRITICAL EYE LOCK:** Both eyeballs remain rigidly fixed in their sockets, maintaining exactly the same orientation relative to the skull throughout the entire orbit. The pupils and irises remain pointed in the exact original direction relative to the face, never tracking or following the camera. The eyelids remain fixed at exactly the same openness as the reference image. Absolutely no blinking, squinting, eye rotation, pupil movement, gaze shifting, eyelid movement or changes in eye shape. As the camera orbits, the apparent gaze direction changes naturally through perspective alone, exactly as it would when walking around a motionless statue.\n\nThe entire face is geometrically rigid. No facial animation, micro-expressions, breathing, head movement, mouth movement, eyebrow movement, hair movement or skin deformation. Preserve the precise original facial identity, expression, geometry, textures and natural photorealistic appearance.\n\nThe subject's head, neck, shoulders, clothing and all surrounding objects remain fixed in world space. The camera alone moves around the stationary subject at constant distance and height, completing exactly one 360-degree horizontal orbit and returning to the identical starting view.\n\nCamera parallax and changing p